From: SupraLINUX Project <packages@supralinux.invalid>
Date: Sun, 01 Nov 2026 21:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] directorysize: do not recurse into other filesystems

Dolphin's Calculate Size action used listRecursive(), which walks into
every mounted filesystem below the selected directory. A calculation on /
therefore entered /proc and counted pseudo-files such as kcore, and could
also walk slow or network mounts.

List one directory at a time and only queue child directories whose
UDS_DEVICE_ID matches the root directory of the calculation. The mount
point directory itself is still counted, but its contents are skipped.
When a protocol does not report device IDs, retain the previous recursive
behaviour.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-01
---
 src/core/directorysizejob.cpp | 51 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 40 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

